-- Fair Trading Act 1986 — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "For this conduct, does it contravene the Act; is it an offence, and up
--    to what fine; is it an infringement offence; may a party seek an order
--    under s 43, and by when; and may only the Commission bring
--    proceedings?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Fair trading position` HAS
    `the conduct contravenes the Act`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is an offence`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `maximum fine`                                      IS A NUMBER
    `it is an infringement offence`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `a party may apply for a s 43 order`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `last day to apply for a s 43 order`                IS A DATE
    `only the Commission may bring proceedings`         IS A BOOLEAN

@ref ss 4, 5D, 7-36ZF, 12C, 15, 40, 40B, 43, 43A
@export default The fair trading position under the Fair Trading Act 1986 (NZ) for one piece of conduct: whether it contravenes the provision engaged (with the in-trade, Crown, news media and s 12A limits), whether that is an offence and the maximum fine (s 40), whether it is an infringement offence (s 40B), whether a party may apply for an order under s 43 (not for s 12A, and not where a valid s 5D clause covers ss 9, 13 or 14(1)), the last day to apply (3 years after the loss was discovered, s 43A), and whether only the Commission may bring proceedings (s 12C). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Conduct case`  @desc The provision engaged and whether the conduct has its quality; whether in trade; the kind of person and whether the Crown; news media facts; any contracting-out clause; the s 12A(3) and s 12D facts; and when the loss was discovered
GIVETH A `Fair trading position`
`the fair trading position for` c MEANS
    `Fair trading position` WITH
        `the conduct contravenes the Act`               IS contravenes
        `it is an offence`                              IS contravenes AND fine GREATER THAN 0
        `maximum fine`                                  IS IF contravenes THEN fine ELSE 0
        `it is an infringement offence`                 IS contravenes AND fine GREATER THAN 0 AND `is an infringement offence` (c's `provision engaged`)
        `a party may apply for a s 43 order`            IS contravenes AND `a party may apply for an order under s 43` c
        `last day to apply for a s 43 order`            IS `the last day to apply for a s 43 order, loss discovered` (c's `loss discovered on`)
        `only the Commission may bring proceedings`     IS c's `provision engaged` EQUALS `s 12A an unsubstantiated representation in trade`
    WHERE
        contravenes MEANS `the conduct contravenes the provision` c
        fine        MEANS `the maximum fine for contravening` (c's `provision engaged`) `, by` (c's `person`) `, the Crown:` (c's `the person is the Crown`)
